{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1s2:000001:issue_created:sase-1s2:94cbf84db9eda268aa7e8cf887c32a6b17bc857766f663d0a360389e36615503","timestamp":"2026-11-08T04:38:03Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rq.2.1.4.1.land","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-1s2","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-1s2","title":"Runner module imports overwrite the process SIGTERM handler","status":"open","issue_type":"task","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-08T04:38:03Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1rq.2.1.4.1.land","updated_at":"2026-11-08T04:38:03Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"Proposed by sase-1rq.2.1.4.1.1 note #2 and independently by sase-1rq.2.1.4.1.3 note #9. At 539afb211e, importing sase.axe.run_agent_runner changes signal.getsignal(SIGTERM) from SIG_DFL to install_sigterm_handler._handler; line 87 installs soft=True at import. mentor_runner.py line 30 likewise installs a handler at import. Install handlers only in the owned runner entry lifecycle, preserving early production signal handling and existing shutdown semantics; imports must not replace the caller handler. Add fresh-interpreter import and real-entry signal tests. Root cause is precise; small scope. Search of all-status tasks and recent tasks found no duplicate; the global-state epic is topical, not the origin of these older side effects.","design":"","model":"","size":"small","task_type":"bug","task_type_fields":{"impact":"Any importing process, including pytest workers, inherits runner-specific signal behavior and can ignore termination.","location":"src/sase/axe/run_agent_runner.py:87; src/sase/axe/mentor_runner.py:30","repro":"In a fresh interpreter, capture signal.getsignal(signal.SIGTERM), import sase.axe.run_agent_runner, and compare: SIG_DFL becomes a soft handler. Seen in monitors kyhnsmgpcjx9 and aa3fzgn042n3 as swallowed SIGTERM."},"is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Contention phases exposed a pre-existing import side effect that makes signal tests order-dependent and can defeat worker teardown. Landing review independently reproduced the handler replacement.","dependencies":[]}}}
